[Megumi] <i>Aw.</i>

462
00:20:14,671 --> 00:20:16,006
What is that? [laughing]

463
00:20:17,216 --> 00:20:18,842
- What is that face?
- "Yeah?"

464
00:20:18,926 --> 00:20:19,968
That grin, yeah.

465
00:20:20,052 --> 00:20:21,929
Like they said,
"Just like that, hold there!"

466
00:20:22,012 --> 00:20:23,305
[laughs]

467
00:20:24,139 --> 00:20:25,349
I'm gonna be sick.

468
00:20:29,311 --> 00:20:30,562
Not here!

469
00:20:30,646 --> 00:20:32,814
- [Awich] <i>He's still looking for them?</i>
- [Nagano] <i>Yeah.</i>

470
00:20:32,898 --> 00:20:34,066
Seriously, what?

471
00:20:35,234 --> 00:20:37,861
There's nobody. Is this a deserted island?

472
00:20:37,945 --> 00:20:39,446
Like, where did they go?

473
00:20:39,529 --> 00:20:41,949
[Megumi] <i>It's a school.</i>
<i>This shouldn't be hard.</i>

474
00:20:42,032 --> 00:20:43,242
How I feel…

475
00:20:44,284 --> 00:20:45,118
hasn't changed.

476
00:20:47,079 --> 00:20:47,955
That's me.

477
00:20:49,289 --> 00:20:50,832
[Ari] What are you doing?

478
00:20:52,209 --> 00:20:53,085
What?

479
00:20:53,168 --> 00:20:55,087
[Ari] What gives?
It's been like five hours!

480
00:20:56,255 --> 00:20:58,799
- [Hikaru] It hasn't been<i> that </i>long.
- I'm crashing this.

481
00:20:58,882 --> 00:21:00,509
- [Hikaru laughs]
- Let's talk.

482
00:21:00,592 --> 00:21:01,426
Okay.

483
00:21:01,510 --> 00:21:02,469
- [Ari] Busy?
- All right.

484
00:21:04,471 --> 00:21:05,681
- Hello.
- Hi!

485
00:21:05,764 --> 00:21:07,599
- Oh, it's nice to meet you, hi!
- Nice, yeah.

486
00:21:07,683 --> 00:21:08,517
I'm Ari.

487
00:21:09,726 --> 00:21:12,562
So, before you said
you weren't interested in anyone, right?

488
00:21:12,646 --> 00:21:14,147
- Mm.
- Still true?

489
00:21:15,065 --> 00:21:16,650
For better or for worse,

490
00:21:17,317 --> 00:21:20,570
I think I've gotten
a little too comfortable around you.

491
00:21:22,948 --> 00:21:24,825
So wait, what does that mean?

492
00:21:24,908 --> 00:21:26,994
It's not like I'm keeping you as a backup.

493
00:21:27,077 --> 00:21:28,662
- I'm really not…
- Doesn't look that way.

494
00:21:28,745 --> 00:21:30,539
…but I'm worried that's how it looks.

495
00:21:30,622 --> 00:21:32,040
But I do worry, so…

496
00:21:32,124 --> 00:21:34,835
But you're still open to considering me,
is that right?

497
00:21:35,419 --> 00:21:36,253
Right.

498
00:21:36,795 --> 00:21:40,132
But I'm seriously thinking about marriage,
so I'm being careful.

499
00:21:43,051 --> 00:21:45,304
Mm, I'm not in love yet.

500
00:21:45,387 --> 00:21:46,388
[Ari] Hmm.

501
00:21:47,639 --> 00:21:49,474
- [Nagano] <i>Hmm, really?</i>
- [Megumi] <i>Oh.</i>

502
00:21:53,270 --> 00:21:55,314
[Leo] I think they're having
a really good date.

503
00:21:55,397 --> 00:21:57,482
[Ruru] It really seems like
they're moving forward.

504
00:21:57,983 --> 00:21:59,109
I bet they kissed.

505
00:21:59,192 --> 00:22:00,360
- [Ari] Really?
- Hope they did.

506
00:22:00,444 --> 00:22:02,863
- [Hikaru] Oh, they're back! Come in!
- We're back!

507
00:22:04,656 --> 00:22:06,408
- [squeals, laughs]
- [Leo] Hey, hey.

508
00:22:06,491 --> 00:22:08,076
[Ma-kun] We're back. What's up?

509
00:22:08,160 --> 00:22:10,370
Oh, nice! Dude, I want to eat too.

510
00:22:10,454 --> 00:22:11,955
- Yeah, I'm hungry.
- [Bou] They did it.

511
00:22:12,789 --> 00:22:14,708
- [Assun] It smells so good.
- [Ma-kun] Good.

512
00:22:14,791 --> 00:22:16,793
- [Assun] Don't crowd us, okay?
- [Maririn] Eat it.

513
00:22:16,877 --> 00:22:17,794
[Ma-kun] It's fine.

514
00:22:17,878 --> 00:22:20,297
- [Hikaru] Did you kiss?
- [both] We didn't.

515
00:22:20,881 --> 00:22:22,257
- Wait, they didn't?
- No way.

516
00:22:22,883 --> 00:22:25,010
Hey, but wait, is that… is that true?

517
00:22:25,093 --> 00:22:26,428
- We didn't. No.
- It's true, right?

518
00:22:26,511 --> 00:22:29,014
- Of course we didn't.
- [Hikaru] Of course you didn't?

519
00:22:29,097 --> 00:22:31,600
- Because our relationship is platonic.
- Platonic.

520
00:22:32,184 --> 00:22:34,311
- Hey do you know what that word means?
- Don't know.

521
00:22:34,978 --> 00:22:36,855
- What's platonic?
- He doesn't know it.

522
00:22:36,938 --> 00:22:39,983
It means pure.
It means we're having a pure relationship.

523
00:22:40,984 --> 00:22:42,527
It's really moving forward.

524
00:22:42,611 --> 00:22:44,029
It's "Badly in Love," right?

525
00:22:44,112 --> 00:22:46,698
[Leo] It's annoying that
you're acting so confident now.

526
00:22:49,576 --> 00:22:52,120
- We were bored, so we came to find you.
- [Bou] Sorry to disturb.

527
00:22:53,205 --> 00:22:54,998
When we were talking to you ladies,

528
00:22:55,624 --> 00:22:57,793
- you shared about domestic violence.
- [Maririn] Right.

529
00:22:57,876 --> 00:23:00,045
- I didn't get what you meant.
- [Maririn] What part?

530
00:23:00,128 --> 00:23:03,757
I guess it's like, the woman gets mad,
but the man gets more in a rage.

531
00:23:03,840 --> 00:23:04,674
[Maririn] Mm-hmm.

532
00:23:04,758 --> 00:23:06,176
But I just don't understand…

533
00:23:07,177 --> 00:23:08,512
why it turns violent.

534
00:23:09,346 --> 00:23:11,723
I was always told that
it was because I didn't listen.

535
00:23:11,807 --> 00:23:13,350
Mm, I was told the same thing.

536
00:23:13,433 --> 00:23:15,602
- So he shut me up.
- I'll say this now, though I know

537
00:23:15,685 --> 00:23:18,980
it makes me look bad,
but when I was young,

538
00:23:19,523 --> 00:23:20,732
- I was cheated on.
- [both] Mm.

539
00:23:20,816 --> 00:23:24,361
And I lost it.
I went blank, and I hit her.

540
00:23:27,906 --> 00:23:29,533
But I don't think I'd…

541
00:23:30,075 --> 00:23:32,327
that I'd ever do it for no reason.

542
00:23:32,410 --> 00:23:33,245
[Ruru] Mm.

543
00:23:33,328 --> 00:23:34,996
I could never hit a woman.

544
00:23:35,622 --> 00:23:37,124
- [Ruru] Mm.
- That's impossible.

545
00:23:37,207 --> 00:23:39,835
Well, you know,
this might just be an excuse,

546
00:23:39,918 --> 00:23:41,920
but I think it was because
I was still young.

547
00:23:42,712 --> 00:23:44,589
- I'd never do that now.
- Mm.

548
00:23:44,673 --> 00:23:47,008
So you hit her and then you realized it?

549
00:23:47,092 --> 00:23:48,969
- Yeah, I knew it was wrong.
- [Maririn] Really?

550
00:23:49,678 --> 00:23:52,180
Mm, I was so frustrated the whole time.

551
00:23:52,264 --> 00:23:55,642
So, then I thought I had to go
and find the guy, and I found him.

552
00:23:59,688 --> 00:24:01,523
- That scared her.
- [Megumi] Yeah, I agree.

553
00:24:01,606 --> 00:24:02,983
She got really scared right there.

554
00:24:03,066 --> 00:24:06,278
But I think it might have been scary
if he'd kept it to himself.

555
00:24:06,361 --> 00:24:07,696
- Right. Hmm.
- That's true.

556
00:24:07,779 --> 00:24:10,740
I do think it was good
that he told them about it.

557
00:24:10,824 --> 00:24:13,118
It really seems like the girls
are the ones in charge.

558
00:24:13,201 --> 00:24:15,162
- In this season, yes.
- [Nagano] In this season.

559
00:24:15,245 --> 00:24:17,372
- The guys are a little bit scared.
- Yes.

560
00:24:17,455 --> 00:24:19,708
- Mm
- Listen, Leo just said "ladies."

561
00:24:19,791 --> 00:24:23,753
- Yes. "Talking with you ladies." [laughs]
- [Nagano] "With you ladies."

562
00:24:23,837 --> 00:24:27,174
- Leo looks like a member of Skapara.
- [laughing]

563
00:24:27,257 --> 00:24:29,634
That looks like a mash-up
of some of the Skapara members.

564
00:24:29,718 --> 00:24:32,679
- [Megumi] He does. I see that.
- [Nagano] Like a blend of all of them.

565
00:24:37,142 --> 00:24:39,436
- [bell chiming]
- [Hikaru] I've heard of it.

566
00:24:39,519 --> 00:24:40,353
MARINE ACADEMY
LOVE

567
00:24:40,437 --> 00:24:42,314
[Ari] To know if you thought it was cool.

568
00:24:43,398 --> 00:24:44,232
I like it.

569
00:24:44,316 --> 00:24:46,735
[boy on PA] <i>Today, we have</i>
<i>an extracurricular activity.</i>

570
00:24:46,818 --> 00:24:48,862
<i>You'll experience traditional</i>

571
00:24:48,945 --> 00:24:51,156
<i>- Okinawan </i>Mouashibi.
- [Awich] What?

572
00:24:51,239 --> 00:24:53,700
<i>This will deepen your bonds</i>
<i>with each other.</i>

573
00:24:53,783 --> 00:24:55,076
- What is it?
<i>- "Mouashibi"?</i>

574
00:24:55,160 --> 00:24:56,244
- What's that?
- [Bou] What?

575
00:24:56,328 --> 00:24:58,830
- Is it okay to do <i>Mouashibi?</i>
- [Nagano] Why? What's <i>Mouashibi?</i>

576
00:24:58,914 --> 00:25:00,415
Is it okay to do <i>Mouashibi?</i>

577
00:25:00,916 --> 00:25:05,503
[boy on PA] Mouashibi<i> is a tradition</i>
<i>passed down through the ages in Okinawa.</i>

578
00:25:06,588 --> 00:25:10,842
<i>This is where young people</i>
<i>would enjoy dancing and singing together,</i>

579
00:25:11,426 --> 00:25:13,678
<i>and hope to find the one they'll marry.</i>

580
00:25:14,846 --> 00:25:16,306
- This is so Okinawa!
- That's amazing.

581
00:25:16,389 --> 00:25:18,308
- Wow, cool. Shiku-wassup!
- Wow.

582
00:25:18,391 --> 00:25:20,769
[Ari] It's Taiko no Tatsujin.
That's awesome.

583
00:25:21,269 --> 00:25:22,854
- [Assun] Whoa.
- [Ma-kun] What?

584
00:25:22,938 --> 00:25:25,023
- [Ari] Sick!
- [traditional music playing]

585
00:25:34,115 --> 00:25:34,950
[Ari] Cool, right?

586
00:25:36,618 --> 00:25:37,619
[Ma-kun] Incredible.

587
00:25:38,161 --> 00:25:39,246
So cool!

588
00:26:04,187 --> 00:26:06,564
- [cheering]
- So great!

589
00:26:06,648 --> 00:26:08,900
Wassup, man!

590
00:26:08,984 --> 00:26:10,318
Whoo!

591
00:26:10,402 --> 00:26:11,861
You guys, that was cool.

592
00:26:11,945 --> 00:26:13,238
- That was crazy!
- Yeah.

593
00:26:13,321 --> 00:26:14,948
- [Bou] Okay, lunch.
- [Ma-kun] Great.

594
00:26:15,031 --> 00:26:17,075
- [Hikaru] What's in there?
- [Ma-kun] Look at this.

595
00:26:17,617 --> 00:26:19,577
- [Assun] Wait, this is crazy.
- [Bou] Whoa.

596
00:26:19,661 --> 00:26:22,163
- [Ruru] Looks delicious.
- [Ari laughing] What? No way!

597
00:26:22,664 --> 00:26:24,374
Should we? All right. One…

598
00:26:24,958 --> 00:26:25,834
two, three…

599
00:26:25,917 --> 00:26:27,669
[all] Wassup!

600
00:26:27,752 --> 00:26:29,879
- [laughter]
- [all] Let's eat.

601
00:26:29,963 --> 00:26:31,131
Dig in.

602
00:26:31,214 --> 00:26:33,925
- Yeah, it's nice.
- So sick! <i>Kakuni.</i>

603
00:26:35,051 --> 00:26:36,428
- [Bou] Good.
- Off the chain, right?

604
00:26:37,095 --> 00:26:38,430
- [Assun] I'm starving.
- Whoa!

605
00:26:38,513 --> 00:26:39,347
[Ari] Crazy, right?

606
00:26:39,431 --> 00:26:41,349
[upbeat music playing]

607
00:26:42,017 --> 00:26:42,934
[Nagano] <i>Oh! What?</i>

608
00:26:43,518 --> 00:26:45,186
- [Awich] <i>A newcomer.</i>
- [Megumi] <i>Mm.</i>

609
00:26:51,443 --> 00:26:52,277
Oh!

610
00:26:53,737 --> 00:26:55,947
- [Ruru] Whoa. Who's there?
- [Bou] What?

611
00:27:07,584 --> 00:27:09,419
- [giggles]
- [Ma-kun] Wassup!

612
00:27:09,502 --> 00:27:11,004
- Wassup, bro!
- [woman] Hello.

613
00:27:11,087 --> 00:27:12,547
- Wassup, wassup!
- [Bou] Hey.

614
00:27:12,630 --> 00:27:14,591
I'm Hazuki, transfer student.

615
00:27:14,674 --> 00:27:16,259
But you can call me Ha-chan. Hi.

616
00:27:16,343 --> 00:27:18,553
- [Ma-kun] Nice to meet you.
- [Tai-chan] Good to meet you.

617
00:27:18,636 --> 00:27:20,221
- [Leo] Welcome.
- [Hikaru] Welcome.

618
00:27:20,722 --> 00:27:21,806
[Ma-kun] Welcome.

619
00:27:21,890 --> 00:27:23,099
HAZUKI ABE
AKA HA-CHAN (27)

620
00:27:23,183 --> 00:27:25,518
I'm Hazuki, I'm 27.
I'm from Miyagi Prefecture.

621
00:27:26,019 --> 00:27:27,228
They call me Ha-chan.

622
00:27:28,063 --> 00:27:30,148
<i>I actually work as a kickboxing trainer.</i>

623
00:27:30,732 --> 00:27:33,818
<i>- I started kickboxing for real at 19.</i>
- [Awich] <i>Awesome.</i>

624
00:27:33,902 --> 00:27:35,320
Compared to most people,

625
00:27:35,403 --> 00:27:38,281
yeah, I think I've definitely
been through hell in my life.

626
00:27:38,365 --> 00:27:41,284
- [Nagano] <i>Oh.</i>
- I was in a center, a children's home.

627
00:27:41,368 --> 00:27:43,078
All of my exes have been arrested,

628
00:27:43,161 --> 00:27:45,747
that's usually why
we'd end up breaking up.

629
00:27:45,830 --> 00:27:47,957
They were arrested for drugs or fraud.

630
00:27:48,041 --> 00:27:50,960
So they'd end up in jail
for three or four years at time.

631
00:27:51,544 --> 00:27:53,129
I want someone who won't get arrested.

632
00:27:54,172 --> 00:27:55,423
It's like a police video.

633
00:27:55,507 --> 00:27:58,051
- I see it.
- [Nagano] With "drugs" and "fraud" there.

634
00:27:58,134 --> 00:27:58,968
DRUGS FRAUD

635
00:27:59,052 --> 00:28:01,554
<i>- It's like a police poster.</i>
- [Megumi] <i>It's a "Just say no" ad.</i>

636
00:28:01,638 --> 00:28:04,224
I want a fair person
with a determined mind.

637
00:28:04,307 --> 00:28:07,185
I don't like when guys look like
a<i> yankii,</i> but really aren't.

638
00:28:07,685 --> 00:28:12,524
I haven't been treated like a woman
for a while, so I forget. [giggles]

639
00:28:12,607 --> 00:28:14,859
So I want a guy to help me remember.

640
00:28:16,111 --> 00:28:17,028
[chuckles]

641
00:28:17,112 --> 00:28:19,114
- Welcome. Wassup?
- [laughs]

642
00:28:19,197 --> 00:28:20,657
- Oh, sorry.
- All good.

643
00:28:20,740 --> 00:28:22,158
Oh, wow. [laughs]

644
00:28:22,242 --> 00:28:23,368
This is intense.

645
00:28:23,451 --> 00:28:25,703
- "Intense" is crazy.
- [Ha-chan] Because you look awesome.

646
00:28:25,787 --> 00:28:28,123
- Are we intense?
- Who has the most intense vibes?

647
00:28:28,206 --> 00:28:29,416
- I don't know.
- You don't?

648
00:28:29,499 --> 00:28:30,625
Well, you.

649
00:28:30,708 --> 00:28:32,961
You look like you used to be a druggie.

650
00:28:33,044 --> 00:28:35,130
- [laughter]
- [Megumi] <i>Choose your words.</i>

651
00:28:35,213 --> 00:28:36,756
- [Ha-chan] Sorry.
- [Ruru] Hey.

652
00:28:37,465 --> 00:28:40,260
- [Megumi] <i>He's not laughing.</i>
- [Nagano] <i>Oh, wow, he didn't laugh?</i>

653
00:28:41,219 --> 00:28:43,930
So now you've seen us,
tell us which guy is your type.

654
00:28:44,514 --> 00:28:45,724
Oh, my type?

655
00:28:46,224 --> 00:28:47,559
I like his face.

656
00:28:47,642 --> 00:28:49,686
- [laughter]
- [Leo] Oh!

657
00:28:49,769 --> 00:28:53,148
- Why, thank you. Thanks.
- I like a genuinely strong guy.

658
00:28:53,231 --> 00:28:56,609
I hate it when guys think they're tough
because they have tattoos,

659
00:28:56,693 --> 00:28:58,194
but really, they're just wimps.

660
00:28:58,278 --> 00:29:00,280
I want a guy who stands up for himself.

661
00:29:00,780 --> 00:29:01,906
That's my type.

662
00:29:05,326 --> 00:29:06,828
- [Megumi] <i>Huh?</i>
- [Nagano] <i>What happened?</i>

663
00:29:07,370 --> 00:29:09,998
- What's going on?
- Gotta sit next to the girl you're into.

664
00:29:10,081 --> 00:29:11,207
That's right.

665
00:29:11,291 --> 00:29:12,584
Let's introduce ourselves.

666
00:29:12,667 --> 00:29:14,169
- [Ha-chan] Yes, please.
- [Bou] Yeah.

667
00:29:14,252 --> 00:29:16,755
- I'm Tai-chan, I'm 22.
- Oh, cool.

668
00:29:16,838 --> 00:29:18,256
Tokyo is home.

669
00:29:18,339 --> 00:29:19,174
- Oh!
- Yeah.

670
00:29:19,674 --> 00:29:21,134
- [Ha-chan] What do you do?
- I do hair.

671
00:29:21,217 --> 00:29:23,303
- Oh. Good to meet you.
- [Tai-chan] Yeah, you too.

672
00:29:23,386 --> 00:29:24,387
[Ruru] Welcome.

673
00:29:24,471 --> 00:29:26,097
- That's in right now.
- Did you see that?

674
00:29:26,181 --> 00:29:28,141
- It's totally a thing.
- [Ari] This is annoying.

675
00:29:28,224 --> 00:29:29,934
- [Leo] Never done it.
- But it has changed.

676
00:29:30,018 --> 00:29:32,187
- [Maririn] Myers-Briggs.
- [Ha-chan] What was it? [sighs]

677
00:29:32,270 --> 00:29:34,063
- [Bou] Did he leave?
- [Leo] He did.

678
00:29:34,147 --> 00:29:35,648
- [Ha-chan] Okay.
- [Maririn] He's upset?

679
00:29:35,732 --> 00:29:37,567
- What's wrong?
- He's really upset.

680
00:29:37,650 --> 00:29:39,402
- [Bou] Hitting the bathroom.
- [Ruru] What?

681
00:29:40,278 --> 00:29:42,363
- He left? [laughs]
- [Assun] He left.

682
00:29:42,447 --> 00:29:44,073
- Is that like him?
- [Ma-kun] He's feeling bad.

683
00:29:50,705 --> 00:29:51,623
[Hikaru] You okay?

684
00:29:51,706 --> 00:29:53,124
- You pissed?
- Yeah, I'm so pissed.

685
00:29:53,208 --> 00:29:55,293
- I mean, I--
- Yeah, I saw your face, man.

686
00:29:55,376 --> 00:29:56,211
- Yeah?
- Uh-huh.

687
00:29:56,294 --> 00:29:59,047
She says I look like I do drugs?
What's wrong with her?

688
00:30:00,215 --> 00:30:03,635
And look, I mean, no one even
comes close to you, Hikaru.

689
00:30:03,718 --> 00:30:06,554
No matter who shows up,
all of them are just duds anyway.

690
00:30:07,263 --> 00:30:09,098
It just made me feel shitty.

691
00:30:09,182 --> 00:30:11,935
Some girl I don't know
calling me a damn druggie.

692
00:30:12,018 --> 00:30:13,311
Yeah, read the room.

693
00:30:14,562 --> 00:30:17,857
A druggie? Is that really wassup? Hell no.

694
00:30:18,733 --> 00:30:19,776
Nah, no wassup.

695
00:30:20,401 --> 00:30:22,237
[laughing] I don't know
what "wassup" means.

696
00:30:22,320 --> 00:30:23,947
- [laughing]
- [Nagano] What's "wassup"?

697
00:30:24,030 --> 00:30:25,448
I don't know what's happening!

698
00:30:25,532 --> 00:30:28,076
- "Is that really wassup?"
- [Nagano] So, "Is that wassup?"

699
00:30:28,827 --> 00:30:31,287
- I wonder how she'll act now.
- Yeah.

700
00:30:36,709 --> 00:30:39,963
[Ha-chan] What's your story, Bou?
How would you describe yourself?

701
00:30:40,046 --> 00:30:43,341
Um, I guess I'd call myself a joker.
In one word.

702
00:30:43,883 --> 00:30:46,344
- Always.
- I bet we're the same age.

703
00:30:47,053 --> 00:30:48,930
- Born in '98?
- Yes, sir.

704
00:30:49,013 --> 00:30:51,724
I'm surprised
there's someone else my age here.

705
00:30:51,808 --> 00:30:54,310
- '98, year of the tiger?
- Year of the tiger.

706
00:30:54,394 --> 00:30:56,437
- Same, same. Yeah.
- [laughs]

707
00:30:56,521 --> 00:30:59,649
- You were arrested?
- For assault and extortion.

708
00:31:00,733 --> 00:31:02,527
Just assault and extortion, huh?

709
00:31:02,610 --> 00:31:04,070
- Yeah, and drugs.
- Hmm.

710
00:31:04,612 --> 00:31:07,574
- What kind of drugs? Meth?
- Uh, yeah.

711
00:31:08,157 --> 00:31:09,742
Right. Okay, show me, then.

712
00:31:12,954 --> 00:31:15,707
- No, I smoked it.
- Oh, yeah? Oh.

713
00:31:18,751 --> 00:31:19,752
[bell chiming]

714
00:31:19,836 --> 00:31:23,423
[boy on PA] <i>Today, we have</i>
<i>the welcome party for the new student,</i>

715
00:31:24,007 --> 00:31:25,008
<i>and you can drink.</i>

716
00:31:25,091 --> 00:31:26,634
- [Ma-kun] Okay, okay.
- [Ha-chan] Yay!

717
00:31:26,718 --> 00:31:29,429
So what kind of things
do you want to know about us?

718
00:31:29,512 --> 00:31:32,140
Tell me everything?
I'm still mixing you guys up.

719
00:31:32,932 --> 00:31:34,809
- I am.
- Should we say our names?

720
00:31:34,893 --> 00:31:36,811
Say your names? Yes, please.

721
00:31:36,895 --> 00:31:38,980
Wait, we did that already. At lunch.

722
00:31:39,647 --> 00:31:43,234
- [Ma-kun] If you forget our names, ask.
- [Assun] It's hard to remember everyone.

723
00:31:45,278 --> 00:31:48,364
- Cheers to us!
- [all cheer]

724
00:31:48,448 --> 00:31:49,282
[Leo] Hey!

725
00:31:51,534 --> 00:31:54,787
[Nagano] <i>It seems like</i>
<i>she's not really accepted yet, right?</i>

726
00:31:54,871 --> 00:31:56,164
[Megumi] <i>Right.</i>

727
00:31:57,373 --> 00:31:59,208
[Ha-chan] I feel like
you're all really bonded.

728
00:31:59,792 --> 00:32:03,212
- Well, I mean, honestly? For real, though?
- [Ha-chan] Mm-hmm.

729
00:32:03,296 --> 00:32:05,506
I can't accept
a transfer student so easily.

730
00:32:05,590 --> 00:32:07,342
Because this all happened fast.

731
00:32:10,011 --> 00:32:12,472
So, I've been living in Tokyo
since I moved there at 20,

732
00:32:12,555 --> 00:32:15,683
and the only people I call my good friends
are from back home.

733
00:32:15,767 --> 00:32:19,020
- [Ha-chan] I see.
- So, I'm not the type to trust easily.

734
00:32:19,896 --> 00:32:22,607
Once we have shared history
and shared lives,

735
00:32:22,690 --> 00:32:25,109
then I usually start to feel like
we can be friends.

736
00:32:25,193 --> 00:32:27,028
I wanted to tell you this in person,

737
00:32:27,111 --> 00:32:29,906
because I don't want to talk
about you behind your back.

738
00:32:29,989 --> 00:32:34,160
I just wanted to be really clear
that I don't trust people easily.

739
00:32:35,745 --> 00:32:37,705
[Megumi] <i>They're hard on the new girl.</i>

740
00:32:39,248 --> 00:32:41,042
[Ruru] Actually,
I want to talk to you alone.

741
00:32:41,125 --> 00:32:42,085
[Ha-chan] Oh, okay.

742
00:32:43,878 --> 00:32:46,422
- I'm feeling confrontational right now.
- Mm.

743
00:32:46,506 --> 00:32:49,884
I can't handle having someone here
who I don't see as one of us.

744
00:32:50,468 --> 00:32:52,804
I get it, but there's no point
in saying that.

745
00:32:52,887 --> 00:32:54,180
- I know there's no point.
- Yeah.

746
00:32:54,263 --> 00:32:58,226
But it's gonna take time
for me to see you as family, Hazuki.

747
00:32:58,309 --> 00:32:59,310
If you can't, you can't.

748
00:32:59,394 --> 00:33:01,437
It's not about whether you can or not.

749
00:33:01,521 --> 00:33:02,897
You don't have the right attitude.

750
00:33:03,481 --> 00:33:07,068
I expect you to say, "But I want
to be family, so I'll work at it."

751
00:33:07,151 --> 00:33:09,028
- That's what I want.
- That's what you wanted.

752
00:33:09,112 --> 00:33:10,363
But that's hard.

753
00:33:10,446 --> 00:33:13,449
I can't just start liking someone
because they ask me to.

754
00:33:13,533 --> 00:33:15,201
I mean, it's fine if you can't do it.

755
00:33:15,284 --> 00:33:18,162
And I don't see someone as family
unless I feel they really are, either.

756
00:33:18,246 --> 00:33:21,165
Oh, see, it's really the same way for you.

757
00:33:21,249 --> 00:33:23,584
You want to know the person first too.

758
00:33:24,168 --> 00:33:26,587
I thought I'd try to be mature
and tell you this.

759
00:33:26,671 --> 00:33:28,172
That's why I wanted to talk.

760
00:33:28,256 --> 00:33:32,260
I can really tell that
you really want to do the right thing.

761
00:33:32,343 --> 00:33:33,469
- [Ruru] Mm.
- Mm.

762
00:33:34,095 --> 00:33:37,724
Today was the first day we met,
and this is my first one-on-one

763
00:33:37,807 --> 00:33:40,101
- with, uh, one of the girls.
- Mm-hmm.

764
00:33:41,769 --> 00:33:43,229
I think we might be the same.

765
00:33:43,312 --> 00:33:46,733
- I know! And I fight with people like me!
- [laughing]

766
00:33:46,816 --> 00:33:50,361
For real, I told them, I never get along
with people who are like me.

767
00:33:50,445 --> 00:33:51,654
I don't.

768
00:33:52,447 --> 00:33:54,866
Yeah, it's pretty hard being
a transfer student.

769
00:33:54,949 --> 00:33:57,285
- [Megumi] <i>Yeah, apparently.</i>
- [Awich] <i>But she faced it well.</i>

770
00:33:57,368 --> 00:33:59,037
[Ha-chan] <i>When I talked with Ma-kun,</i>

771
00:33:59,537 --> 00:34:03,249
<i>he said I should apologize to Ari</i>
<i>for saying that he looked like a druggie,</i>

772
00:34:03,332 --> 00:34:04,417
<i>and he's right.</i>

773
00:34:05,043 --> 00:34:07,920
So, I wanted to go
and find Ari to apologize.

774
00:34:08,004 --> 00:34:09,881
[door opens]

775
00:34:09,964 --> 00:34:11,799
- Ari, you have a sec?
- [Ari] Who, me?

776
00:34:11,883 --> 00:34:12,717
[Ha-chan] Yeah.

777
00:34:14,302 --> 00:34:16,971
- There's something I want to talk about.
- Oh, yeah?

778
00:34:17,055 --> 00:34:20,058
So, you know that
I really got thrown into things today.

779
00:34:20,141 --> 00:34:21,017
Mm-hmm.

780
00:34:21,100 --> 00:34:24,771
And so when you
were sitting next to me at lunch,

781
00:34:24,854 --> 00:34:28,191
- I said, "You look like a druggie."
- Ah.

782
00:34:28,274 --> 00:34:31,986
And I said it as a joke.
It really was meant as just a joke.

783
00:34:32,070 --> 00:34:34,739
- Huh. Mm.
- I wasn't serious, at all.

784
00:34:34,822 --> 00:34:37,200
And I wanted to apologize.

785
00:34:37,283 --> 00:34:38,493
Oh, okay.

786
00:34:38,576 --> 00:34:40,161
- I wanted to say that.
- Oh, is that it?

787
00:34:40,661 --> 00:34:42,830
So, my ex was a druggie,

788
00:34:42,914 --> 00:34:45,958
and, um, he ended up
choking and suffocating me.

789
00:34:46,042 --> 00:34:49,837
Honestly, I have a lot of trauma from that

790
00:34:49,921 --> 00:34:52,298
- and I shouldn't pass judgment onto you.
- Yeah.

791
00:34:53,132 --> 00:34:54,592
So, in the rap scene, right?

792
00:34:55,218 --> 00:34:59,180
It's a common thing.
Super common, really. It's everywhere.

793
00:34:59,263 --> 00:35:00,598
Lots of druggies.

794
00:35:01,140 --> 00:35:03,434
One of my old rapper friends did drugs.

795
00:35:04,018 --> 00:35:05,728
That guy was a real addict,

796
00:35:06,395 --> 00:35:08,648
and he had a ton of overdoses,

797
00:35:08,731 --> 00:35:10,525
and he was wanted by the police.

798
00:35:11,067 --> 00:35:14,487
One time, we had a meeting
before a concert, and the cops came.

799
00:35:15,446 --> 00:35:18,741
They took him away,
and they made me take a urine test.

800
00:35:18,825 --> 00:35:19,951
Mm-hmm.

801
00:35:20,034 --> 00:35:23,037
They took me
to the police station, interrogated me,

802
00:35:23,121 --> 00:35:25,665
and, oh, man, the concert was canceled.
That happened a lot.

803
00:35:26,833 --> 00:35:29,627
And I was like,
"What's the point of this?", right?

804
00:35:29,710 --> 00:35:33,047
- Right, when you're working so hard.
- He's messing things up for his friends.

805
00:35:33,131 --> 00:35:35,383
So I've really hated drugs,

806
00:35:35,466 --> 00:35:37,009
- ever since then.
- You hate them.

807
00:35:37,093 --> 00:35:40,179
And a lot of my work
comes from the city government,

808
00:35:40,263 --> 00:35:42,974
so I make sure not to do that stuff.

809
00:35:43,057 --> 00:35:45,184
I don't even go to places
where it's happening.

810
00:35:45,268 --> 00:35:47,311
- Oh, I feel really bad now. [sighs]
- So…

811
00:35:47,395 --> 00:35:49,230
- No, no, it's okay.
- Uh-huh.

812
00:35:49,313 --> 00:35:51,107
- How'd you know if I hadn't told you?
- Right.

813
00:35:51,190 --> 00:35:54,777
And you apologized,
so I won't hold it against you.

814
00:35:55,361 --> 00:35:58,906
I just really… I wanted you
to understand that I went through that.

815
00:35:59,532 --> 00:36:00,741
Yeah, I'm sorry.

816
00:36:00,825 --> 00:36:02,076
- No, it's okay.
- I really am.

817
00:36:02,160 --> 00:36:03,703
- [Megumi] <i>Good apology.</i>
- [Awich] <i>Yeah.</i>

818
00:36:03,786 --> 00:36:05,913
You've changed my impression of rappers.

819
00:36:07,498 --> 00:36:10,251
- He changed her impression of rappers.
- Good to hear.

820
00:36:10,334 --> 00:36:12,170
- [laughing]
- [Nagano laughs] "Good to hear."

821
00:36:12,253 --> 00:36:13,880
- That's good to hear, but…
- Yeah.

822
00:36:14,380 --> 00:36:16,591
Is it true that rappers
are associated with drugs?

823
00:36:16,674 --> 00:36:18,384
Yeah, yeah. That's true.

824
00:36:18,467 --> 00:36:22,680
Back in the '80s, when hip-hop
was really just starting to take off…

825
00:36:22,763 --> 00:36:23,598
[Megumi] Mm-hmm.

826
00:36:23,681 --> 00:36:26,225
- …drugs were already a major problem.
- [both] Mm.

827
00:36:26,309 --> 00:36:28,477
And there was a lot violence too.

828
00:36:28,561 --> 00:36:30,646
Racial and economic discrimination

829
00:36:30,730 --> 00:36:32,815
was still prevalent
in a lot of the United States,

830
00:36:32,899 --> 00:36:35,318
so, as a way to escape from all that,

831
00:36:35,401 --> 00:36:38,279
rap developed as
an artistic medium of expression.

832
00:36:38,362 --> 00:36:41,157
It was a way of escaping
what was happening in life.

833
00:36:41,240 --> 00:36:43,492
And performers would rap
about their experiences.

834
00:36:43,576 --> 00:36:44,410
[both] Mm.

835
00:36:44,493 --> 00:36:46,913
So because they were saved by the music…

836
00:36:46,996 --> 00:36:49,040
- [Megumi] Right.
- …they tended to think it was good,

837
00:36:49,123 --> 00:36:52,960
that whole kind of attitude around it,
and um, it still remains.

838
00:36:53,044 --> 00:36:54,545
- [Megumi] Mm.
- Yeah, I see.

839
00:36:54,629 --> 00:36:57,215
So, now that we have Ha-chan too,
how will they--

840
00:36:57,298 --> 00:37:00,301
- You said Ha-chan, I heard "antisocial".
- [laughing]

841
00:37:00,384 --> 00:37:02,511
I thought,
"Okay, that's where we are now."

842
00:37:02,595 --> 00:37:04,889
- It's not.
- See, they're not all like that.

843
00:37:04,972 --> 00:37:06,599
- Antisocial people.
- Not antisocial.

844
00:37:06,682 --> 00:37:07,725
- We don't know.
- Excuse me,

845
00:37:07,808 --> 00:37:10,019
- but even at Netflix, that's not allowed.
- I'm sorry.

846
00:37:11,729 --> 00:37:13,147
- [Assun] Oh!
- [Leo] Whoa! Nice!

847
00:37:13,231 --> 00:37:14,273
- No, no--
- Get it.

848
00:37:14,357 --> 00:37:15,441
One more time. That's mine.

849
00:37:15,524 --> 00:37:18,194
- [Leo] Go.
- [Hikaru] Yeah, I'm no match for you, sis.

850
00:37:18,945 --> 00:37:21,489
- No, you can't.
- Can I stand here?

851
00:37:21,572 --> 00:37:22,782
- No, please!
- All right?

852
00:37:22,865 --> 00:37:24,867
- Wait.
- Stop flirting.

853
00:37:25,618 --> 00:37:27,411
- [Awich] <i>Whoa.</i>
- [Megumi] <i>Getting close. Wow.</i>

854
00:37:27,495 --> 00:37:28,621
She's really cute.

855
00:37:29,121 --> 00:37:30,790
<i>When she came over to me, like that,</i>

856
00:37:31,832 --> 00:37:34,168
<i>it's not "like" anymore. It's "love."</i>

857
00:37:35,253 --> 00:37:37,463
<i>She totally stole my heart.</i>

858
00:37:38,130 --> 00:37:40,049
<i>Today, and tomorrow too.</i>

859
00:37:40,925 --> 00:37:42,093
I'm Ruru crazy.

860
00:37:42,593 --> 00:37:43,552
Cheers!

861
00:37:50,142 --> 00:37:51,727
[imperceptible]

862
00:37:52,853 --> 00:37:55,815
- [Awich] <i>Oh, that's nice.</i>
- [Nagano] <i>Wow, that's nice! For rivals.</i>

863
00:37:56,816 --> 00:37:58,526
[Megumi] <i>He's a hairstylist, you know.</i>

864
00:38:00,486 --> 00:38:02,571
- Thank you, Taisei.
- [Tai-chan] You got it.

865
00:38:05,324 --> 00:38:07,952
- [Nagano] <i>He's refreshing.</i>
- [Megumi] <i>He looks good when working.</i>

866
00:38:08,035 --> 00:38:09,537
- [Nagano] <i>Yeah!</i>
- [Megumi] <i>Mm.</i>

867
00:38:09,620 --> 00:38:12,748
[Ari] I didn't expect this hairstylist
with so many tattoos.

868
00:38:12,832 --> 00:38:14,166
- [Ma-kun] Me neither.
- [Ari] Yeah.

869
00:38:14,250 --> 00:38:15,876
[Leo] I thought he was a rapper.

870
00:38:15,960 --> 00:38:18,462
- Really? "You did?"
- [Leo] Yeah, I thought, "Really? Is he?"

871
00:38:18,963 --> 00:38:21,382
Same, I thought,
"Why are there so many rappers?"

872
00:38:21,465 --> 00:38:23,175
- Rapper, yakuza, rapper.
- [Ari] Really?

873
00:38:23,259 --> 00:38:24,093
And that was it.

874
00:38:24,969 --> 00:38:26,762
- You're done.
- [Ma-kun] Thank you.

875
00:38:26,846 --> 00:38:28,973
- [Ari] True! That's cool.
- [Ma-kun] I'm different now.

876
00:38:29,056 --> 00:38:30,141
[Ari] Yo, yo, yow!

877
00:38:30,725 --> 00:38:32,727
[bell chiming]

878
00:38:36,814 --> 00:38:39,233
- [boy on PA] <i>A new student is coming.</i>
- Again?

879
00:38:39,817 --> 00:38:41,485
- [Ha-chan] Wait, what?
- [Hikaru] Wait. Shh!

880
00:38:41,569 --> 00:38:42,653
What? For real?

881
00:38:42,737 --> 00:38:45,323
<i>Everyone, please go welcome them</i>
<i>in the classroom.</i>

882
00:38:45,406 --> 00:38:46,615
- [Hikaru] What?
- [Assun] Now?

883
00:38:46,699 --> 00:38:47,533
[Maririn] A guy?

884
00:38:48,284 --> 00:38:51,495
- Could it be another guy?
- Woo-hoo!

885
00:38:51,579 --> 00:38:52,663
- Woo-hoo!
- [laughing]

886
00:38:52,747 --> 00:38:55,875
- [whooping excitedly]
- [Ha-chan laughing] She's crazy.

887
00:38:55,958 --> 00:38:57,960
[rap music playing]

888
00:38:58,044 --> 00:39:00,546
- [Awich] <i>It's a guy.</i>
- [Nagano] <i>Whoa, look at this guy!</i>

889
00:39:02,048 --> 00:39:03,591
<i>Uh-oh, he looks handsome.</i>

890
00:39:05,634 --> 00:39:07,720
[music continues]

891
00:39:11,390 --> 00:39:15,311
BADLY IN LOVE
MARINE ACADEMY

892
00:39:17,104 --> 00:39:19,023
[imperceptible]

893
00:39:27,281 --> 00:39:28,240
[Awich] <i>What was that?</i>

894
00:39:28,324 --> 00:39:30,910
<i>- What reaction was that?</i>
- [Megumi] <i>Oh, she thinks he's hot.</i>

895
00:39:31,619 --> 00:39:32,912
[Ruru] Oh.

896
00:39:35,039 --> 00:39:36,082
Hello.

897
00:39:36,165 --> 00:39:38,417
Uh, I'm Kazuma Shioda.

898
00:39:38,918 --> 00:39:39,794
Thank you.

899
00:39:40,669 --> 00:39:42,671
[dramatic music playing]

900
00:39:43,964 --> 00:39:45,132
People call me Kazu-kun.

901
00:39:45,216 --> 00:39:46,300
KAZUMA SHIODA
AKA KAZU-KUN (29)

902
00:39:46,384 --> 00:39:49,178
I run a… a host club.

903
00:39:50,596 --> 00:39:53,182
I've been living alone all my life

904
00:39:53,265 --> 00:39:56,060
and I'd say violence,
uh, it's basically all around me.

905
00:39:56,560 --> 00:39:57,436
Women?

906
00:39:58,145 --> 00:39:59,230
Always like me.

907
00:39:59,814 --> 00:40:00,648
How many women?

908
00:40:01,273 --> 00:40:02,149
Don't remember.

909
00:40:03,025 --> 00:40:06,070
You don't remember how many times
you've eaten meat, right?

910
00:40:07,279 --> 00:40:08,155
I'm hot.

911
00:40:09,490 --> 00:40:10,324
I have money.

912
00:40:10,825 --> 00:40:11,992
I'm funny.

913
00:40:12,076 --> 00:40:13,035
And I'm kind.

914
00:40:14,036 --> 00:40:16,330
I like my face, yeah. Mm.

915
00:40:16,956 --> 00:40:18,833
When I wake up, I'm glad to be me.

916
00:40:19,875 --> 00:40:22,336
It's good to be me. [laughs]

917
00:40:23,129 --> 00:40:25,631
- Oh, man, we've got a wild one!
- Okay, thank you.

918
00:40:25,714 --> 00:40:26,799
He's speaks his mind.

919
00:40:26,882 --> 00:40:28,759
Ruru was reacting so much.

920
00:40:28,843 --> 00:40:29,885
- See that?
- [Megumi] Right.

921
00:40:30,469 --> 00:40:32,930
[Nagano] <i>Do you all really act</i>
<i>like this?</i> [laughs]

922
00:40:33,013 --> 00:40:35,224
Like an old lady watching a Korean star?

923
00:40:35,307 --> 00:40:37,393
[mockingly] "Oh, what do I do?
A cute boy is here."

924
00:40:37,476 --> 00:40:39,603
It's fine when she's young,
but you can imagine

925
00:40:39,687 --> 00:40:41,188
what she'll be like when she's older.

926
00:40:41,272 --> 00:40:44,483
- I bet she'll be obsessed with Korea!
- [both laughing]

927
00:40:44,567 --> 00:40:46,193
But isn't she being too obvious?

928
00:40:46,694 --> 00:40:48,028
Do they know each other?

929
00:40:48,946 --> 00:40:50,614
I'm 29 years old…

930
00:40:50,698 --> 00:40:52,616
KAZU-KUN (29)
TOKYO - HOST CLUB OWNER

931
00:40:52,700 --> 00:40:54,243
…from Toyama Prefecture.

932
00:40:55,494 --> 00:40:59,373
And I'm here for love,
so, I won't be friends with the guys.

933
00:41:04,253 --> 00:41:05,921
So, girls, nice to meet you.

934
00:41:06,005 --> 00:41:08,757
- Nice to meet you too.
- [Ari] Then go home. Go home.

935
00:41:09,758 --> 00:41:13,137
'Cause you don't have a room, chump. What?
You don't want friends?

936
00:41:13,721 --> 00:41:15,848
- I don't.
- [Ari] You don't have a room, bitch.

937
00:41:15,931 --> 00:41:17,808
- What're you gonna do? You brat.
- Sit down.

938
00:41:17,892 --> 00:41:18,976
Huh? What?

939
00:41:19,518 --> 00:41:22,104
- Sit down.
- I said you don't have a room, punk. Hey.

940
00:41:22,188 --> 00:41:23,898
Are you a freakin' punk? Huh?

941
00:41:25,483 --> 00:41:27,401
- [Megumi] <i>Ari's never like this.</i>
- [Nagano] <i>Yeah.</i>

942
00:41:27,485 --> 00:41:30,154
- [Ari] Piece of crap.
- [Nagano] He's the feel-good guy.

943
00:41:33,532 --> 00:41:35,534
[bell chiming]

944
00:41:39,914 --> 00:41:41,624
[boy on PA] <i>Attention, boys.</i>

945
00:41:41,707 --> 00:41:43,375
<i>To welcome the new student,</i>

946
00:41:43,876 --> 00:41:46,712
<i>please work together</i>
<i>to make him a welcome dinner.</i>

947
00:41:47,630 --> 00:41:49,131
There's no way I'm doing that.

948
00:41:49,882 --> 00:41:53,385
You'll make your own dinner,
because you don't have any friends.

949
00:41:54,011 --> 00:41:54,845
Clear?

950
00:41:56,055 --> 00:41:57,389
You were told, so make it.

951
00:41:58,390 --> 00:42:01,352
Only if I agree, right? I didn't agree.

952
00:42:01,435 --> 00:42:03,229
You said you don't want to make friends.

953
00:42:03,312 --> 00:42:04,313
- [Kazu-kun] Mm.
- Huh?

954
00:42:05,064 --> 00:42:07,650
- So why would I do that?
- Just do what you're told.

955
00:42:07,733 --> 00:42:09,151
You make it. Yeah?

956
00:42:10,152 --> 00:42:11,320
- You were told to.
- [Bou] You!

957
00:42:12,279 --> 00:42:13,239
The hell?

958
00:42:14,907 --> 00:42:15,741
Hey!

959
00:42:16,617 --> 00:42:18,160
- [Megumi] <i>Uh-oh.</i>
- Make your own dinner.

960
00:42:18,244 --> 00:42:19,245
[Nagano] <i>Whoa!</i>

961
00:42:19,328 --> 00:42:20,287
You make it.

962
00:42:22,873 --> 00:42:24,917
- [Megumi] <i>Oh, no. Oh, my.</i>
- [Nagano] <i>Here they go.</i>

963
00:42:25,000 --> 00:42:27,253
[dramatic music playing]

964
00:42:29,338 --> 00:42:31,048
[Ma-kun] Go outside. Go outside.

965
00:42:36,262 --> 00:42:37,763
Okay, wait, wait, wait.

966
00:42:38,597 --> 00:42:39,890
Okay, fine. Chill a sec.

967
00:42:40,599 --> 00:42:41,433
[Bou] Sorry.

968
00:42:41,976 --> 00:42:42,893
[Ma-kun] You okay?

969
00:42:43,602 --> 00:42:45,104
- Are you okay?
- I went flying.

970
00:42:45,187 --> 00:42:46,146
[Bou clears throat]
